## Phase model v4 (development; `code/e4_theory.py: phase_model_v4`)

v4 keeps v3's closed forms and carries the event loop past the first crossing. Each direction is in one of three
states, re-read after every event:

- **Collapsed** (h < 0, or |a| below the seed amplitude): A-ii' collapse wait to the stability loss, re-seed, then an
  exact burst segment (600 steps).
- **Hover** (inside the window, below thr): A-iii' wait, either to thr (then settled) or to p's edge of stability
  (then an exact chatter segment, 1500 steps).
- **Captured** (|a| > thr): an exact post-crossing segment (600 steps). This segment carries the burst's throw of p
  and any second collapse. After it, a direction above thr with p inside the window is settled: by A-iv' it is alive
  iff c/s > thr from then on. Otherwise it re-enters the loop.

At most 12 events per direction are allowed; at the cap the settled law applies. No constant was fitted to a grid.
The segment lengths only set where the exact map hands back to the closed forms. Varying the post-crossing segment
over 300-3000 steps moves dev3's rank-within-1 failure from 0.0644 to 0.0639 and leaves dev2's unchanged
(`results/e4/dev*/v4_dev_score.txt`, `code/checks/e4_dev_v4_on_grid.py`).

